rrier (grey block), expanding into circular wave fronts. Arrows indicate the direction of wave travel (upwards and outwards).\n        *   No explicit text labels inside this specific diagram other than the arrows.\n\n    *   **Bottom Left Diagram (Reflection visual):**\n        *   Label: \"Reflection\" (top left of this sub-box).\n        *   Labels: \"\\(i^o\\)\", \"\\(r^o\\)\" (angles).\n        *   Label: \"Reflecting surface, e.g. shiny object or mirror\" (bottom).\n        *   Visual: A green line (incident ray) hitting a horizontal black line with diagonal hash marks (reflecting surface). A dashed vertical line (normal) is at the point of incidence. Another green line (reflected ray) bounces off. Arrows indicate direction.\n\n    *   **Bottom Middle Block (Rule):**\n        *   Text: \"All wave can be reflected and refracted\"\n\n    *   **Bottom Middle Block (Law of Reflection):**\n        *   Text: \"Law of Reflection:\"\n        *   Text: \"Angle of incidence = Angle of Reflection\"\n\n    *   **Bottom Right Block (Diffraction Rules):**\n        *   Text: \"Maximum diffraction occurs when: the gap is equal to the wave.\"\n        *   Text: \"Minimum diffraction occurs when: the gap is smaller or larger than the wave.\"\n\n3.  **Structure and Format the Output (in Chinese):**\n    *   Translate the structure into Markdown headings.\n    *   Keep English text exactly as it appears.\n    *   Group by main concepts (Central, Top Left, Middle Left, Top Middle, etc.) or follow a logical flow. Grouping by the main topics (Refraction, Reflection, Diffraction) works best.\n\n    *   *Drafting the Markdown structure:*\n\n        *   **主标题 (Main Title)**\n            *   P1c: Reflection, Refraction, Diffraction\n\n        *   **折射 (Refraction)**\n            *   定义: REFRACTION: Bends the wave when entering/leaving a substance to another\n            *   解释: They slow down because the substance would be a different density to another substance.\n            *   图示 (D